  "text": "GPT Directly Controls Blender Inside Cursor\n\nStar_Knight12 · x · 2026-07-13\n\nA reply shares a hands-on test: the author prompted GPT-5.6-Sol directly within Cursor to set up Blender MCP, successfully creating and rendering a \"realistic floating MacBook.\"\n\nThe author emphasizes having never opened Blender before, but with these tools, you can essentially \"grab the docs, pick an IDE, and start building.\" The key highlight is that the combination of MCP + IDE + models is already capable of running a 3D toolchain.\n\nRelated event: Beginner Runs Blender Rendering via Cursor and MCP(9 posts)→\n\nOriginal post →\n\nMore from coding & agent\n\nAI-built bbtree claims fastest concurrent btree; researcher calls for ambitious academic systems — tianyin_xu · 2026-10-25\n\nOctopus OS: a 45k-line Rust kernel where agents rewrite their own harness mid-task — _AustinCalvert_ · 2026-10-25\n\nDev argues Rust would be better if modules, not crates, were the compilation unit — zetalyrae · 2026-10-25\n\nDev open-sources BizAgent framework where one AI lead agent manages a dozen AI employees — Low-Start2333 · 2026-10-25\n\nFormal Verification Yields to Static Analysis, Which Yields to Better Language Design — xennygrimmato_ · 2026-10-25\n\nScanning 115,798 agent ledger rows: zero capability revocations, none with expiry — Affectionate-Sun265 · 2026-10-25\n\ncoding & agent channel →",
